And it was so funny because
she was attacking me

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:46.020
'cause I wanted to leave,
it was getting too much.

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:48.980
I wanted to go to rehab and
get myself clean and just get

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.820
away from her 'cause she
was physically attacking me.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:55.120
And so when I actually called
the cops, got out of the house

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:57.670
I started detoxing,
learning about other people

00:11:57.670 --> 00:12:00.090
who's got it way worse than me,

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:03.260
but like still is in the same area as me.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:06.500
And I got to actually learn
what my problems were,

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:07.700
how to get out.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:12.570
But I got sidetracked by raving,
which I got to be med tent,

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:16.450
but I also fell into all
the drugs that raves do

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:18.800
enable you to have and
they're right there.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:22.270
But once I started
messing with psychedelics,

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:23.930
I was like, this is a problem,

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.230
because you do get in your head.

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:27.220
And I was like, my body is skinny,

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:31.710
I'm losing weight, not gaining
it, pills are a problem.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:36.710
And December 24th of 2019, I
just gave pills up cold turkey,

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:39.050
went through the whole detox,
went through everything.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:41.800
And I was like, "I don't
wanna end up where my mom is."

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:46.750
She has four girls and all of
them are kind of questioning

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.030
how they messed up so much

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:52.460
when we didn't really do anything wrong.

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:54.600
We're a child, we're here just to learn

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:57.850
and we had to teach and learn ourselves.

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:58.970
- [Interviewer] So you're clean now?

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:01.040
- Oh yeah, I'm clean 100%.

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:04.660
I have on my phone these calendar,
like these clocks of days

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:08.310
of everything that I
stopped using what days,

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:12.850
and there's nothing under
100 right now, or even 170.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.560
And I'm so excited about that
'cause it's such a hard thing

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:18.410
to talk about, is the shame of drug abuse.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:21.150
And it's like, somebody
like me, they could probably

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:25.870
see me as a stoner, yeah, I
give off those vibes 100%,

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:29.620
but no one knew that I was
abusing Norcos and even Percosets

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:34.270
no one really knew that
my friend was doing lines,

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:37.110
she was snorting Xanax, and
she was doing lines like this,

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:40.740
and I would cut it in half
because she would overdose.

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:44.300
And it was really hard
because I had to give up

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:47.260
a whole friendship and
friend group to get sober

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:49.270
and to even help my friend get sober

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:51.300
'cause she was doing lines of coke.

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:55.070
And I almost overdosed in her
house just from half a line

00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:57.660
she was doing, and she
was doing more than me.

00:13:57.660 --> 00:14:00.180
And I didn't even do coke,
I was doing her Xanax lines.

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:03.030
So I was like, "Oh my gosh,"
I was like, "I can't do it."

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:05.890
And I even lost that friendship.

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:10.150
But it's like the whole drugs are just,

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:11.950
they affect you so
differently in the shame

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:16.690
just you never actually reach
out until you hit rock bottom.

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:18.520
But I've gone to NA meetings.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:21.020
They've actually really saved a lot of,

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:22.810
they've wasted so much
of my time sometimes,

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:26.640
but it just gives me another
reason to want to help people

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.350
who are in those situations.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:32.080
Like on my Twitter, I may have
like 1,000 followers already

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:33.620
but I'll still message people back.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:37.560
I've had people say, "Hey, I'm
having a suicide problems."

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:40.140
I'm like, I don't care, Raven is here.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:41.700
I'm still talking to you right here,

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:44.010
but if you want my personal
information, I'm here just

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.940
because I know how hard
it is not to have anyone,

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.500
especially like I had my nana and my mom,

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:53.030
but my nana would tell me straight,

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:57.740
and she passed away this
last June, or no July,

00:14:57.740 --> 00:14:59.800
this last July of 2020.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:03.010
So I haven't really had
her to help keep me going

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:06.430
or my mom, but my mom
was my enabler as well

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:10.130
and basically my supplier to all my drugs.

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.360
And it was really hard
when I stopped doing them

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:14.690
because they're right there,
I could still do them.

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:16.430
She has them in the house, but it's like-

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:17.940
- [Interviewer] And also using today?

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:21.290
- She uses Suboxone, which
is a lower form of opioid.

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:24.730
But to be honest, she
really does stockpile them

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:27.200
and doesn't use them or
she'll overuse one day

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.690
'cause she's in more pain and I'm like,

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:32.640
that's just the addiction
because you don't really need

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:35.890
all these boxes of drugs for
possible future outcomes,

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:38.270
that's just like the shame you have.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:41.680
And we get into massive
arguments over it 'cause she says

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:45.020
that she's clean, she's doing
fine, but you're not clean

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:47.210
if you're still using
it and making excuses.

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:50.310
And it's so hard 'cause
I know my mom and I

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:52.760
will never have that
relationship that I really envy,

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:53.640
that everyone has.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.590
Like I'll see TikToks of
people with their moms

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:59.420
and I'm like, man, if I
did TikToks people would be

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:02.900
really depressed and I'd go
viral for another reason.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:06.480
And it's like I do have to
record my mom's arguments in mind

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:11.480
because she does invalidate
all my experiences I've had.

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:15.780
And I wouldn't be where I am
now if I didn't have them.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:18.780
And everyone who has those relationships,

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:20.800
at least, even if they are drugged ones

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:23.030
and they have close
relationships with their family,

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:26.470
I really envy that just because I had that

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:30.090
with both of my grandmothers
and now they're gone.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:32.497
And it's like so hard,
'cause people are like,

00:16:32.497 --> 00:16:33.697
"I've lost my mother," and I'm like,

00:16:33.697 --> 00:16:36.750
"Me too, but my biological
one's still alive."

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:38.850
And it's hard 'cause people
don't understand that.

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:42.850
But my eldest sister and
I have talked about it

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.780
and it's got like we
agree that we lost our mom

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.250
a long time ago.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:49.870
And she's still trying to find herself

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:51.720
but we can't really help her with that.

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:55.710
And that's the hardest
part about at least me

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:57.660
'cause everyone's like, "Oh,
go talk to your mom," or this.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:58.910
And I'm like, "Okay."

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:02.640
- [Interviewer] Change's a big
part of addiction, isn't it?

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:03.473
- It is.

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:06.610
I didn't go to my mom.

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:09.850
Even though she was the
one giving it to me,

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:10.850
I would go to my nana,

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:12.780
she was the only person
that had no shame on it.

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:14.680
But I never really went
to my friends for help

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:19.680
until I was like skinny, I
wasn't eating, I wasn't hungry.

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:24.260
I was detoxing completely,
I lost like 10 pounds,

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:26.800
and it just completely changed me.

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:28.777
And I was so shameful just to tell people,

00:17:28.777 --> 00:17:30.260
"Yeah, I'm detoxing from drugs,"

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:33.550
until one day I just got
so fed up with people

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:35.730
expecting me to help them
and be in their lives.

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:39.594
And I'm like, I'm trying to
get my shit together myself.

00:17:39.594 --> 00:17:42.310
I'm like, what am I supposed to do?

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:44.167
So I just told people, I'm like,

00:17:44.167 --> 00:17:45.827
"Hey, I'm going through
this problem right now.

00:17:45.827 --> 00:17:49.247
"I'm addicted to pills
and I can't help anyone

00:17:49.247 --> 00:17:50.860
"until I help myself."

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:53.960
And it was at that moment
that I lost so many people.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.680
So many people just
stopped being my friend.

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:57.610
They were like, "Oh, you're
no fun, you're a prude."

00:17:57.610 --> 00:18:00.610
I'm like, "Yeah, I am,
I'll take it, I'm a prude."

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:04.797
But I got closer with so many
other people who were like,

00:18:04.797 --> 00:18:07.300
"I actually wanna quit too
and I'm having a struggle."

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:10.590
And that's when I got this
really good group of friends

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:13.370
that I just acquired and
I'm working hard to keep

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.850
just because it's a lot of work.

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:19.690
And when I was on drugs, I just
didn't care if I had friends

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:22.210
I would talk to them like they
were my best friends ever,

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:24.910
but in reality, we had
no clue about each other.

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:28.480
And getting over that shame
really brought the real people,

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:30.980
the genuine friends that I have out.

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:32.840
And it just takes that like big step

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:35.890
of getting over your
own fears and boundaries

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:39.033
just because you're your own
worst enemy during those times.

00:18:40.257 --> 00:18:41.715
- [Interviewer] So then at
some point you got to...

00:18:41.715 --> 00:18:42.548
How old are you?

00:18:42.548 --> 00:18:43.530
- I'm only 20.

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:44.363
- [Interviewer] You're 20.

00:18:44.363 --> 00:18:45.880
So you've been through
a lot for a 20-year old.

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:46.713
- Oh yeah.

00:18:46.713 --> 00:18:48.520
- [Interviewer] And then you
got into porn at some point.

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:50.990
- I got into porn when I was 19.

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:54.590
Last year actually I was, for
the pandemic when that started

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:59.190
I got kicked out because my
mom listened to a conversation

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:01.210
and (chuckles) she

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:05.980
listened to me talking
about my past drug use

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:10.690
and me talking to someone
privately just about help.

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:11.930
And I was getting off the shame.

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:15.910
She kicked me out dramatically
and very traumatically.

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:20.910
And that is when I actually
started getting things together.

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:23.480
But then it was a pandemic.

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.680
So there's not a lot of things open,

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.120
everything was going down,
and I said, you know what?

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.210
I've been saying this since
I was young, if I have

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:32.550
no other option, why not be
a stripper or a porn star?

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:35.540
And I was just joking, but
I was serious at that point.

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:37.970
And I was like, you know
what, I'm really hypersexual.

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:41.000
I take pride in actually pleasing someone.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.990
I've had an OnlyFans for a little bit

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.880
and I'm comfortable with it, I was like,

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:46.460
you know what, I'm gonna try it.

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:49.230
And so I just went on to
Pornhub out of everything

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:50.587
and I noticed there's like,

00:19:50.587 --> 00:19:52.120
"Wanna join the talent, sign here."

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.940
And I clicked on one of them.

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:57.780
And in April I got just a call back

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.330
from Backroom Casting Couch.

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:02.530
And that's when they were like,
we would love to have you.

00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:04.947
And I was just so shocked
that somebody was like,

00:20:04.947 --> 00:20:07.320
"Yeah, your pictures that
you sent in were beautiful."

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:11.080
And I was like, you
know what, it's $2,000.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:13.220
I didn't get a stimulus, I was a student.

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:15.430
I was like, I need this
money just to live.

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:16.960
And I was like, it'll help me out.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:18.920
I was like, it's a one-time
thing, no contract signed.

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:20.610
I was like, and if I like it, I like it,

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.600
if I don't, never again.

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:25.210
And it ended up being
such an amazing thing.

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:26.980
They paid for my flights and everything,

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:28.660
which usually doesn't happen.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:31.600
But it was just such
an amazing experience.

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:33.890
And just to get money
for actually doing work

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:36.120
and helping out and being genuine,

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:39.040
I was like, this is so amazing.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:41.640
And during the pandemic,
it helped out so much

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:43.240
'cause I didn't have my parents,

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:48.250
I applied for loans and I
couldn't even get loans or grants.

00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:53.250
I was working three jobs
and it was just right when

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:57.260
I did that, I was like, you
know, this might be something.

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:59.680
And I didn't think anything of it.

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:01.730
I kind of let my ego
get to it a little bit,

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:05.260
but then I got a call a week
later from the same people.

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:06.557
And they're like, "Hey,
we had someone cancel,

00:21:06.557 --> 00:21:07.857
"would you like to do another shoot?

00:21:07.857 --> 00:21:10.160
"This is a one-time thing,
we don't usually offer this."

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:11.630
And I was like, "Yes, let me take it."

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.370
I didn't even care about the
offer, I didn't even care,

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:14.870
I was like, "I will be there ASAP,"

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:17.150
I got on a plane the next morning.

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:19.730
And I was like, this is
something that I wanna do,

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:22.880
I like traveling, I like
having to actually keep

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:26.950
a good image on my body and
work harder for what I want.

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:29.750
Because yeah, I could pay for
someone to make me beautiful

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:32.200
but working hard for it
and having people be like,

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:35.630
you're genuinely beautiful
and hear it all the time,

00:21:35.630 --> 00:21:38.040
at least in the industry really

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:40.330
gave me the confidence I needed.

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:44.600
And after my nana died few
months later, I was like,

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:46.990
I fell into a depression work-wise,

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:49.160
it was even worse for COVID,

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:52.287
and that's when I just get
a call and they were like,

00:21:52.287 --> 00:21:53.937
"Do you wanna actually be in the industry,

00:21:53.937 --> 00:21:56.420
"it's calming down, we can
get you in and do shoots."

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:59.120
And I went, "Yes," without a hesitation.

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:02.050
I started working up just
to drive down to L.A.,

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:04.580
and I actually ended up flying,

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:08.440
and it just became such
a good experience for me

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:11.480
just because I got to witness
what it would actually be like

00:22:11.480 --> 00:22:13.750
and see if I could actually handle it.

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:15.610
And at first it was really scary

00:22:15.610 --> 00:22:17.080
just to have all these cameras on me,

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:19.190
all these people looking at
me telling me how to pose,

00:22:19.190 --> 00:22:21.290
telling me how to look
and not even knowing

00:22:21.290 --> 00:22:23.840
what pictures would come
out, and having just

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:27.810
this little insecurity
that I've had for so long.

00:22:27.810 --> 00:22:30.970
And it just all washed away.

00:22:30.970 --> 00:22:34.080
And now that I'm in it, it
just makes me so excited.

00:22:34.080 --> 00:22:36.920
'Cause there's been so many
influences to steer me away

00:22:36.920 --> 00:22:39.360
from being where I'm at right now.

00:22:39.360 --> 00:22:41.570
Like my parents don't
agree with it at all.

00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:43.860
I get called a whore and
a slut, and I get told

00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:47.730
that I'm gonna be on crack
by the time I get here.

00:22:47.730 --> 00:22:50.690
And it's so hard because
these are my parents

00:22:50.690 --> 00:22:52.170
telling me these things.

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:54.070
And all my friends are really supportive.

00:22:54.070 --> 00:22:55.727
They're like, "As long as you're safe,

00:22:55.727 --> 00:22:57.647
"as long as it's everything
good and you're happy,

00:22:57.647 --> 00:22:58.500
"that's all I want."

00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:00.510
And I'm like, "Aw."

00:23:00.510 --> 00:23:01.580
I'm happy where I'm at,

00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:03.160
I'm getting somewhere where I want to be,

00:23:03.160 --> 00:23:07.220
and then it's like, I
let family overshadow

00:23:07.220 --> 00:23:08.800
the actual people that are important.

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:11.630
And listening to people that are important

00:23:11.630 --> 00:23:14.290
have really gotten me to where I am today.

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:17.610
And I'm not hesitant, I'm
really excited to wear...

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:20.090
Like I get a text about a
shoot and if I can't make it

00:23:20.090 --> 00:23:23.080
just because I'm too far
