00:35:31.750 --> 00:35:34.470
Especially in L.A., there's so
many people going through it

00:35:34.470 --> 00:35:37.610
during COVID and it just
breaks my heart that

00:35:37.610 --> 00:35:40.040
they may reach out or they may not

00:35:40.040 --> 00:35:41.730
and they have to go through this.

00:35:41.730 --> 00:35:44.830
And not enough people are
aware of the signs of people

00:35:44.830 --> 00:35:48.123
going through stuff just because
we're so good at hiding it.

00:35:49.100 --> 00:35:54.100
And as much as I love people
who don't go through this stuff

00:35:54.400 --> 00:35:57.580
I just hate the ignorance
that sometimes comes

00:35:57.580 --> 00:35:59.770
just of like, you have no clue

00:35:59.770 --> 00:36:02.933
what that person has gone
through and it's been hell.

00:36:03.800 --> 00:36:05.937
People have threatened to
beat me up and I've gone,

00:36:05.937 --> 00:36:09.510
"My mother can probably do
better than you, I'm sorry."

00:36:09.510 --> 00:36:12.200
Like you're nowhere
compared to where this woman

00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:15.690
or like any of my exes could be.

00:36:15.690 --> 00:36:18.373
And for people who just
don't go through it,

00:36:19.260 --> 00:36:22.610
I just always recommend taking a step back

00:36:22.610 --> 00:36:26.830
for some situations and always
thinking before you speak,

00:36:26.830 --> 00:36:31.830
just because some people
really are not there

00:36:31.980 --> 00:36:34.970
when they're going through
it and it's so hard

00:36:34.970 --> 00:36:38.080
to not project when you've
just gone through something

00:36:38.080 --> 00:36:41.490
or not shut down or go
into a depressive episode.

00:36:41.490 --> 00:36:43.700
And it's like, these
things are so normal to me,

00:36:43.700 --> 00:36:44.790
and when my friends go through it,

00:36:44.790 --> 00:36:45.800
there'll be depressed on the couch.

00:36:45.800 --> 00:36:48.040
I'll be cleaning their house
and I'll just be taking care

00:36:48.040 --> 00:36:51.280
of them because I know it's
something that's normal.

00:36:51.280 --> 00:36:52.900
And it's like the shame
that comes with it,

00:36:52.900 --> 00:36:55.170
even people just go through something,

00:36:55.170 --> 00:36:56.640
never gone through
something in their life,

00:36:56.640 --> 00:36:59.713
get shameful that bad
things happen to them.

00:37:01.360 --> 00:37:04.240
It's not really your fault,
it's out of your control

00:37:04.240 --> 00:37:07.010
unless you're an addict taking pills,

00:37:07.010 --> 00:37:09.670
you know it's your fault,
you just need the support.

00:37:09.670 --> 00:37:11.270
And that's what I've been
lacking my whole life,

00:37:11.270 --> 00:37:14.510
is outside support
'cause I've just had me.

00:37:14.510 --> 00:37:18.240
And now that I have it,
it's such a difference.

00:37:18.240 --> 00:37:21.630
I tried rejecting it at first
'cause that's what people do

00:37:21.630 --> 00:37:25.330
but once you accept it and
you know your boundaries

00:37:25.330 --> 00:37:28.960
and you learn yourself and how
you can function with others

00:37:28.960 --> 00:37:32.170
without being scared of your past traumas,

00:37:32.170 --> 00:37:34.150
it really does help people.

00:37:34.150 --> 00:37:35.670
Especially if you've never gone through it

00:37:35.670 --> 00:37:38.150
you can see a different
change with someone

00:37:38.150 --> 00:37:40.880
once you've resolved or
at least got some closure

00:37:40.880 --> 00:37:42.432
to something that's been bugging them.

00:37:42.432 --> 00:37:43.355
- [Interviewer] With therapy.

00:37:43.355 --> 00:37:44.188
- With what?

00:37:44.188 --> 00:37:45.021
- [Interviewer] With therapy.

00:37:45.021 --> 00:37:47.010
- Oh yeah, therapy or even
just talking to a friend

00:37:47.010 --> 00:37:49.300
and actually having a
real sit-down not like,

00:37:49.300 --> 00:37:52.020
oh my God, that's so funny, LMA, whatever.

00:37:52.020 --> 00:37:53.490
Having a real sit down with people

00:37:53.490 --> 00:37:57.090
and just talking, like
communicating not with a phone

00:37:57.090 --> 00:37:59.090
which is so hard during COVID.

00:37:59.090 --> 00:38:01.430
And that's why so many other
people are having depression

00:38:01.430 --> 00:38:04.463
and families are arguing and
I've seen so many TikToks

00:38:04.463 --> 00:38:07.287
with people just like,
"Yay, my mom's abusive again

00:38:07.287 --> 00:38:08.120
"'cause I moved back."

00:38:08.120 --> 00:38:11.150
I'm like, (sighs) "I
understand it completely."

00:38:11.150 --> 00:38:13.600
And that's something that I
hate that I can understand,

00:38:13.600 --> 00:38:16.160
is I know if I ever have a kid

00:38:16.160 --> 00:38:18.450
is that that's never gonna happen,

00:38:18.450 --> 00:38:22.790
is that unwanted feeling
or that just fear.

00:38:22.790 --> 00:38:25.700
And that's where a lot of
people can empathize with me,

00:38:25.700 --> 00:38:27.830
is that they don't
respect a lot of people,

00:38:27.830 --> 00:38:29.180
they fear a lot of people

00:38:29.180 --> 00:38:32.126
just because you can't
gain fear with respect.

00:38:32.126 --> 00:38:32.970
- [Interviewer] What do
you think the difference is

00:38:32.970 --> 00:38:35.110
between people who

00:38:37.060 --> 00:38:40.220
end up broken from the
childhoods like yours

00:38:40.220 --> 00:38:41.750
and people like yourself who maybe

00:38:41.750 --> 00:38:43.840
have climbed out of it
and become stronger?

00:38:43.840 --> 00:38:46.600
- The worst-case scenario
that I've just seen

00:38:46.600 --> 00:38:47.670
are serial killers happen.

00:38:47.670 --> 00:38:50.240
And if you look at them, they're way high.

00:38:50.240 --> 00:38:53.970
But if you look at them as
the worst-case scenario,

00:38:53.970 --> 00:38:55.740
they've been through troubled childhood.

00:38:55.740 --> 00:38:59.190
Some have not, but a lot
of people who do crimes

00:38:59.190 --> 00:39:02.930
or even kill others have such emotional,

00:39:02.930 --> 00:39:05.160
like emotions just bottled up

00:39:05.160 --> 00:39:07.540
from their emotional abuse and trauma.

00:39:07.540 --> 00:39:10.250
And I've looked at so many people,

00:39:10.250 --> 00:39:12.130
they wouldn't have done
drugs if they didn't have

00:39:12.130 --> 00:39:14.700
this influencer there, or this stressor.

00:39:14.700 --> 00:39:19.700
And it's just so much because
it's right then and there.

00:39:21.230 --> 00:39:23.690
And if you can't reach
out 'cause you're shameful

00:39:23.690 --> 00:39:27.910
or you don't know that it's
this traumatic for you,

00:39:27.910 --> 00:39:31.260
you're gonna do something
stupid by all means.

00:39:31.260 --> 00:39:34.280
Or you're gonna end up like me hopefully.

00:39:34.280 --> 00:39:36.700
Or you're gonna be lost for a while.

00:39:36.700 --> 00:39:40.200
And it does feel really
harsh to just not really

00:39:40.200 --> 00:39:42.360
know what you're doing,
kind of learning yourself.

00:39:42.360 --> 00:39:44.270
And that's why I did all of last year,

00:39:44.270 --> 00:39:46.180
is I would just cry and cry.

00:39:46.180 --> 00:39:48.150
Even when I started here, I'd just cry

00:39:48.150 --> 00:39:51.150
because life is so hard.

00:39:51.150 --> 00:39:53.940
But I wasn't reaching
out like I thought I was

00:39:53.940 --> 00:39:55.467
until somebody said, "You
haven't talked to me,

00:39:55.467 --> 00:39:56.300
"why didn't you reach out?"

00:39:56.300 --> 00:39:59.140
I'm like, "Oh gosh," I was
like, "because I'm depressed."

00:39:59.140 --> 00:40:00.360
What am I supposed to do?

00:40:00.360 --> 00:40:03.160
And once I can joke
about it and get over it

00:40:03.160 --> 00:40:05.363
and even realize what I'm doing,

00:40:06.370 --> 00:40:09.690
like transparency with people,
at least I can handle it

00:40:09.690 --> 00:40:11.330
as people will be like, "You're
depressed, get out of bed."

00:40:11.330 --> 00:40:12.820
I'll be like, "Oh, you're right."

00:40:12.820 --> 00:40:15.610
But some people really
need that support system

00:40:15.610 --> 00:40:18.610
that I never had or
that I was that person,

00:40:18.610 --> 00:40:20.770
but never got it back.

00:40:20.770 --> 00:40:24.090
And so with that, it's just
there's so many different ways

00:40:24.090 --> 00:40:28.500
people could end up because
if you let it prolong

00:40:28.500 --> 00:40:31.130
and you don't actually
acknowledge the problems

00:40:31.130 --> 00:40:34.430
or you don't cope with it
and your body just one day,

00:40:34.430 --> 00:40:36.380
you get mad cause you
can't close a drawer.

00:40:36.380 --> 00:40:39.730
And you're mad about
everything last past 20 years.

00:40:39.730 --> 00:40:42.650
That's a worst-case scenario
for a normal person,

00:40:42.650 --> 00:40:45.150
but then there's serial
killers or even people

00:40:45.150 --> 00:40:47.610
who kill themselves
because it's just so much.

00:40:47.610 --> 00:40:50.570
And mental health, at least
right now I've noticed,

00:40:50.570 --> 00:40:52.640
it's just not taken seriously anymore.

00:40:52.640 --> 00:40:56.290
'Cause everyone has
depression, everyone has this,

00:40:56.290 --> 00:40:58.230
everyone's having problems
but it's just because

00:40:58.230 --> 00:41:01.040
we have literally no
support system during COVID.

00:41:01.040 --> 00:41:03.320
We're all locked away from each other,

00:41:03.320 --> 00:41:05.910
and people don't wanna be
on their phones as much

00:41:05.910 --> 00:41:08.600
'cause that's all we have is
to connect with each other.

00:41:08.600 --> 00:41:11.010
And I think this last
year and still going on

00:41:11.010 --> 00:41:13.210
is gonna be the hardest mentally at least

00:41:13.210 --> 00:41:16.260
'cause no person expected a pandemic,

00:41:16.260 --> 00:41:18.000
no one expected to change their life

00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:21.280
or go back to an old life
they had abandoned like I did.

00:41:21.280 --> 00:41:24.870
And it's so hard, especially since

00:41:24.870 --> 00:41:26.910
everyone's going through this nationwide.

00:41:26.910 --> 00:41:29.500
And at least for me, I know
I have cried multiple times

00:41:29.500 --> 00:41:32.790
from it and I've stressed,
cried, just screamed in my car

00:41:32.790 --> 00:41:35.507
and just had moments
where I'm like, "Why?"

00:41:36.410 --> 00:41:40.210
And it's just the support
system I think people need

00:41:40.210 --> 00:41:45.210
to either end up on a
really outbursts spectrum

00:41:45.270 --> 00:41:48.770
of a meltdown or a more calm burnout.

00:41:48.770 --> 00:41:50.690
And that's where I think
everyone was this year,

00:41:50.690 --> 00:41:54.690
is just burnt out, too much
working, too little working.

00:41:54.690 --> 00:41:55.840
It was just so much stress.

00:41:55.840 --> 00:41:58.350
Everyone had to change their life

00:41:58.350 --> 00:42:00.860
for either the best or
the worst at the time.

00:42:00.860 --> 00:42:02.380
And that's all we had to deal with,

00:42:02.380 --> 00:42:04.490
and it was out of our control.

00:42:04.490 --> 00:42:07.610
And at least with me, I
know that I can empathize

00:42:07.610 --> 00:42:10.500
with people during COVID
because it is so much

00:42:10.500 --> 00:42:14.570
and it's so beautiful
just to like, oh gosh,

00:42:14.570 --> 00:42:17.330
with someone I'd never
think that I would be

00:42:17.330 --> 00:42:19.410
sympathizing and empathizing with

00:42:19.410 --> 00:42:21.960
actually turn into a
really good friend of mine.

00:42:21.960 --> 00:42:25.010
And they may have followers,
thousands of followers,

00:42:25.010 --> 00:42:29.170
and just because I reached out
one day and this one follower

00:42:29.170 --> 00:42:31.250
just had a feeling that they were not okay

00:42:31.250 --> 00:42:33.650
and now we're friends and it's like,

00:42:33.650 --> 00:42:38.280
wow, we really don't reach
out as much as we do.

00:42:38.280 --> 00:42:41.020
And that's where the
shame just comes back in.

00:42:41.020 --> 00:42:43.604
And once you just literally take it off,

00:42:43.604 --> 00:42:44.800
it's literally just like a cloak,

00:42:44.800 --> 00:42:46.870
you just take it off and it's gone.

00:42:46.870 --> 00:42:48.890
That's why I have no shame at my doors,

00:42:48.890 --> 00:42:51.370
no shame in my car, no shame anywhere.

00:42:51.370 --> 00:42:53.080
You shouldn't have shame for anything

00:42:53.080 --> 00:42:56.070
unless you're doing something wrong.

00:42:56.070 --> 00:42:58.240
And that's at least what I felt growing up

00:42:58.240 --> 00:43:00.953
and probably how everyone feels as well.

00:43:01.890 --> 00:43:02.723
- [Interviewer] All right, Raven.

00:43:02.723 --> 00:43:04.031
Well, thank you so much
for sharing your story,

00:43:04.031 --> 00:43:04.864
very interesting.
- Yeah, thank you

00:43:04.864 --> 00:43:05.790
for having me.

00:43:05.790 --> 00:43:07.590
- [Interviewer] Thank you very much.

